From: somestupidgirl <sunnevanattsol@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] vim: build without the private WeakLinking.h

os_mac_conv.c includes <SoftLinking/WeakLinking.h>, which only the
internal SDK carries, for one line: WEAK_LINK_FORCE_IMPORT of
CreateTextEncoding(), which keeps the weak import in the binary for
systems that lack the function.  Every macOS this builds for has it, and
the declaration comes from the public Carbon headers either way, so the
line is kept where the header exists and left out where it does not.

--- a/src/os_mac_conv.c	2026-09-14 23:53:52
+++ b/src/os_mac_conv.c	2026-09-14 23:53:52
@@ -24,8 +24,10 @@
 
 #if defined(MACOS_CONVERT) || defined(PROTO)
 
+#if __has_include(<SoftLinking/WeakLinking.h>)
 #include <SoftLinking/WeakLinking.h>
 WEAK_LINK_FORCE_IMPORT(CreateTextEncoding);
+#endif
 
 # ifdef PROTO
 // A few dummy types to be able to generate function prototypes.
